{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "39107f64-8531-8d39-a259-2e2985d32f4e",
  "created_at": "2025-12-29T12:28:54-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Janice Lawton",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:25:54-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Lorraine. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:25:59-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, sorry, I know this is silly, but I have a couple of questions about recycling. What's allowed now?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:26:07-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not silly at all. What are you wondering about?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:26:11-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, so, pizza boxes. Can those go in the recycling bin? Sometimes they have grease on the bottom."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:26:18-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, pizza boxes. Generally the clean cardboard part is fine, but the parts soaked with grease should go in the regular trash. A lot of people tear off the clean lid and recycle that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:26:31-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, okay. Sorry, I've just been putting the whole thing in. And glass? Do jars and bottles still go in with everything else?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:26:40-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, glass bottles and jars go in the recycling. Empty them and give them a quick rinse. Lids can stay on."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:26:48-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. I know this is silly, but what about those plastic clamshells, the ones the berries and salad come in?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:26:56-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The clamshells. Those are the ones where I'd say check the number on the bottom and the current list the city puts out. I don't want to tell you wrong on those. I can mail you the list or you can look on the city website under recycling."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:27:14-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, yes, could you mail it? That'd be great."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:27:18-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. I'll need your address. Where are you located?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:27:22-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's 228 Gibbs Avenue, on the Ocean Drive side."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:27:26-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Two twenty-eight Gibbs Avenue. And the name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:27:30-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Janice Lawton. L-A-W-T-O-N."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:27:32-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Janice Lawton, L-A-W-T-O-N, 228 Gibbs Avenue. I'll get that out to you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:27:37-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. Sorry, one more. When is my next pickup? With the holidays I've lost track."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:27:44-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me look at your street. [pause] Okay, Gibbs Avenue. Are you trash and recycling both?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:27:51-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, both. Same day, I think. Sorry, I should know this."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:27:56-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. Your pickup is Thursday this week, January first, but the holiday can shift things. Let me double check. [pause] Yes, holiday schedule has you moving to Friday, January second."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:28:08-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Friday the second. Okay, so I put the bins out Thursday night."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:28:13-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thursday night or early Friday morning, either way. Friday, January second, for both trash and recycling."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:28:20-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect. Sorry, I'm also trying to get organized because I'm planning a family reunion for next summer, and I'm in charge of everything. Lots of paper plates and bottles, so I wanted to know the rules."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:28:34-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's a good thing to sort out ahead of time. Bottles and clean cardboard are fine, and the list I'm mailing will help you with the rest."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:28:45-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. Thank you so much for your help."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:28:49-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Janice. Have a good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-29T12:28:52-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye."
    }
  ],
